course: dictionary
lesson: 13185
title: Science words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Friction is the force that slows things down when two surfaces rub together. Frictional is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It means caused by friction, or to do with friction. You can spot the link: friction, plus the ending -al, which means "to do with".
explain: «The frictional force between the tyres and the road slowed the bike.» Frictional tells you the force comes from friction. Ask: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence: "the force caused by rubbing between the tyres and the road" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: Surfaces matter. «Sandpaper is rough, so it creates a lot of frictional force.» A smooth, polished table creates much less. Science words often describe what you can see happening, so look for the action in the sentence: here, things are rubbing.
explain: «Rubbing your hands together makes frictional heat, so they feel warm.» Here frictional heat is the heat made when two surfaces rub. Scientists use the same word in the same way, so once you know it in one lesson, you can use it in others.
fact: Friction is the force that slows things down when surfaces rub together.
fact: Frictional means caused by friction, or to do with friction.
fact: A «frictional force» acts against movement.
fact: Rough surfaces give more friction than smooth ones.
fact: Brakes, shoe grips and tyres all use frictional forces to work.
exercise: «The frictional force between the tyres and the road slowed the bike.» What does frictional mean here? | Caused by a magnet | *Caused by friction | Caused by a loud noise | Caused by bright sunshine
exercise: Which surface would give the most frictional force? | *A sheet of rough sandpaper | A tray of cold, clean ice | A smooth glass window | A smooth, polished table
exercise: «Rubbing your hands makes frictional heat.» Find and copy the word that tells you the heat comes from friction. | *frictional | heat | hands | rubbing
test: Which word means to do with friction? | *Frictional | Frictionless | Fictional | Fractional
test: Why do your hands feel warm after you rub them together? | Because they are wrapped in warm gloves | Because the sun is shining on them | Because they are touching ice | *Because frictional heat is made when they rub
exam: Which sentence uses frictional correctly? | *«Brakes use frictional forces to slow the car.» | «The frictional sky was bright blue.» | «The frictional cat ran across the garden.» | «She frictional the cake for tea.»
